==English==

===Etymology===
First attested about 1860, in the US, as a fanciful alteration of {{term|lick}} and the verb {{term|split}}. {{term|lick}} appears to have something to do with animals made to go faster by means of a "lick" of a whip, although it may have also originated due to a preference for rapid licking (the "quick lick").

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-lickety-split.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|head=[[lickety]]-[[split]]|-}}

# [[quickly|Quickly]]; as [[fast]] as possible; in short order.
#: ''At the sound of the starting gun, they were off and running '''lickety-split'''.''

